AIM
To develop a webpage using JavaScript for form validation and DOM manipulation.


PROCEDURE
1. Create an HTML registration form.
2. Add Name, Email and Age input fields.
3. Write JavaScript using DOM methods.
4. Validate the entered details using conditional statements.
5. Display error or success messages after submission.
6. Save as 3.html and test the form.

PROGRAM
Save the following code as 3.html and open it in a web browser.

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>JavaScript Form Validation</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f2f2f2;
            padding: 30px;
        }
        .container {
            width: 350px;
            margin: auto;
            padding: 25px;
            background-color: white;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }
        input, button {
            width: 100%;
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 8px 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        button {
            background-color: #333;
            color: white;
            border: none;
        }
        #message {
            margin-top: 15px;
            font-weight: bold;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h2 id="heading">Registration Form</h2>

        <form id="myForm">
            <label>Name:</label>
            <input type="text" id="name">

            <label>Email:</label>
            <input type="text" id="email">

            <label>Age:</label>
            <input type="number" id="age">

            <button type="submit">Submit</button>
        </form>

        <p id="message"></p>
    </div>

    <script>
        // DOM Manipulation
        document.getElementById("heading").textContent = "User Registration";

        // Form Validation
        document.getElementById("myForm").addEventListener("submit", function(event) {
            event.preventDefault();

            let name = document.getElementById("name").value;
            let email = document.getElementById("email").value;
            let age = document.getElementById("age").value;
            let message = document.getElementById("message");

            if (name === "") {
                message.textContent = "Please enter your name.";
                message.style.color = "red";
            }
            else if (email === "" || !email.includes("@")) {
                message.textContent = "Please enter a valid email.";
                message.style.color = "red";
            }
            else if (age === "" || age < 18) {
                message.textContent = "Age must be 18 or above.";
                message.style.color = "red";
            }
            else {
                message.textContent = "Registration Successful! Welcome " + name;
                message.style.color = "green";
            }
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>

OUTPUT
The registration form is displayed with Name, Email and Age fields.
- Empty name: “Please enter your name.”
- Invalid email: “Please enter a valid email.”
- Age below 18: “Age must be 18 or above.”
- Valid details: “Registration Successful!”

RESULT
Thus, form validation and DOM manipulation were successfully performed using JavaScript methods such as getElementById(), textContent, style and addEventListener().
